&Q000453

{A.1 = 1-15}
A.1.	Shrine of @wSN{Nibru}, shrine surpassing the @fsux{abzu}, 
A.2.	shining @wTN{E-kur}; 
A.3.	your prince is the Great Mountain @wDN{Enlil} who surpasses the Prince @noteref{i.e. @wDN{Enki}}. Your great lady is the good woman, 
A.4.	Mother @wDN{Ninlil}, excelling in refinement. 
A.5.	Your caretaker is one whose vigour is surpassing, the hero @wDN{Ninurta}. 
A.6.	The chief minister @noteref{i.e. @wDN{Nuska}}, who is worthy of your fair copper vessels, 
A.7.	who makes your bedchamber exceedingly pleasant, 
A.8.	is also the guardian watching over your honourable divine powers; 
A.9.	he is the shepherd watching over your honourable divine powers. 
A.10.	Your provider, 
A.11.	who was engendered by the Great Mountain and was born by @wDN{Ninlil} -- @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, 
A.12.	who was engendered by the Great Mountain, 
A.13.	and was born by @wDN{Ninlil}, 
A.14.	he who has achieved a high reputation among his numerous people, 
A.15.	throws himself at your feet. 

{A.11 = 11-16}
A.11.	@wSN{Nibru}, your praise suits the mouth! May it be uttered by every mouth! 
A.12.	The @wDN{Anuna} gods always stand by your truthful utterances. 
A.13.	Shrine @wSN{Nibru}, primeval city, 
A.14.	where the divine powers are allotted, sweet is your praise! 
A.15.	At the great festivals prepared with care in @wSN{Nibru}, 
A.16.	all the great gods …… the majesty of @wDN{Enlil} and @wDN{Ninlil}. 

{A.17 = 17}
A.17.	@fsux{Sa-gida}. 
